   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "School science in Spanish",
     "texto": [
      "Today we talk about shapes, science and space.\n\n- **Shapes:** a **círculo** (round), a **triángulo** (triangular), a **cuadrado** (square), a rectangle (rectangular).\n- **The four operations:** sumar, restar, **multiplicar** and **dividir**. They are read like this: tres **más** dos son cinco · cinco **menos** dos son tres · tres **por** dos son seis · seis **entre** dos son tres.\n- **States of matter:** **sólido**, **líquido** and **gas**. Water **se congela** (freezes) and **se evapora** (evaporates).\n- **Materials:** **hierro** (iron), gold, glass, wood. The material is said with **de**: una puerta **de hierro**.\n- **Science:** physics, chemistry, a **método**, an experiment.\n- **Space:** the **atmósfera** surrounds the Earth; an astronaut travels in a rocket; a **satélite** orbits a planet."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Processes with «se»",
     "texto": [
      "To talk about natural processes, Spanish uses **se** with the third person of the verb. Nobody does the action: it just happens.\n\n- El agua **se congela** a cero grados.\n- El hielo **se derrite** con el calor.\n- El agua del mar **se evapora**.\n\nIf there are several things, the verb is plural: **se congelan** los lagos; **se evaporan** los charcos.\n\nCompare: **yo congelo** la comida (I do the action); la comida **se congela** (it happens to it)."
     ],
